From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:05:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Do not unref the worker thread after joining it

g_thread_join() drops the reference the caller holds, so the
g_thread_unref() after it reads freed memory. valgrind reports it at daemon
shutdown (invalid read in g_thread_unref, block freed by g_thread_join). ASan
does not, because the read is in uninstrumented glib.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/worker_routine.c
+++ b/src/worker_routine.c
@@ -59,7 +59,6 @@
 	if (self->thrd)
 	{
 		g_thread_join(self->thrd);
-		g_thread_unref(self->thrd);
 		self->thrd = NULL;
 	}
 
